  "_approach": "Two-bar 32nd-grid micro-rush build: bar 1 keeps the 4/4 kick and clap while the snare enters in 16ths at beat 3; bar 2 thins the kick to beats 1 and 3 and the snare accelerates from 16ths into 32nds with velocity ramping to 127, then stops dead for the last two 32nds - the silence gap before the bass drop. Ref: Notion and Skepsis drop transitions, Darkzy 'Wobble'. (re-voiced for the Vermona DRM1 MKIII's 8 channels)",
